  { p: 'Who was Menander (Milinda)?', op: ['A Tamil poet', 'The founder of the Satavahana dynasty', 'A Kushana emperor', 'An Indo-Greek king who converses with the monk Nagasena'], certa: 3, exp: 'Menander I was an Indo-Greek king of the northwest and the protagonist of the Questions of Milinda.' },
  { p: 'What does the inscription on the pillar of Heliodorus, at Vidisha, say?', op: ['That Ashoka became a Buddhist', 'That a Greek was a devotee of Vasudeva (Krishna)', 'That Rome sent envoys to India', 'That Kanishka founded an era'], certa: 1, exp: 'Heliodorus, ambassador of Antialcidas, raised the pillar in honour of Vasudeva, «god of gods», and calls himself a «bhagavata».' },
  { p: 'How was the Buddha represented at Bharhut and on the gateways of Sanchi?', op: ['By golden statues', 'By portrait paintings', 'By symbols (tree, wheel, footprints, stupa)', 'He was never represented, not even by symbols'], certa: 2, exp: 'Until the 1st century AD the Buddha appears mostly through symbols; the human image comes with Gandhara and Mathura.' },
  { p: 'Which dynasty dominated the Deccan from the 1st century BC and patronised caves such as those of Karli?', op: ['Kanvas', 'Licchavis', 'Satavahanas', 'Pallavas'], certa: 2, exp: 'The Satavahanas ruled the Deccan and lived from trade with the west and the sea.' },
  { p: 'The Rabatak inscription, in Bactrian, which gives the genealogy of the kings, was ordered by which emperor?', op: ['Ashoka', 'Kanishka', 'Samudragupta', 'Pushyamitra'], certa: 1, exp: 'The Rabatak inscription is Kanishka’s and names his ancestors: Kujula Kadphises, Vima Takto and Vima Kadphises.' },
  { p: 'What is the name of the 1st-century AD text that describes ports and goods between the Red Sea and India?', op: ['Arthashastra', 'Naturalis Historia', 'Ptolemy’s Geography', 'Periplus of the Erythraean Sea'], certa: 3, exp: 'The Periplus of the Erythraean Sea, by an anonymous author, c. AD 40 – 70, is a guide to navigation and trade.' },
  { p: 'What does the Muziris papyrus record?', op: ['A Sangam poem', 'A loan secured on the cargo of a ship coming from India', 'A peace treaty between Rome and India', 'A list of Kushana kings'], certa: 1, exp: 'The papyrus, from the 2nd century, records a contract linked to the ship Hermapollon, which was coming from Muziris to Alexandria.' },
  { p: 'Which script of northwest India was written from right to left?', op: ['Brahmi', 'Devanagari', 'Tamil', 'Kharosthi'], certa: 3, exp: 'Kharosthi, derived from Aramaic, was used in the northwest; Brahmi was written from left to right.' },
  { p: 'Which Kshatrapa king had a long Sanskrit inscription engraved at Junagadh, c. AD 150?', op: ['Nahapana', 'Gondophares', 'Rudradaman', 'Kharavela'], certa: 2, exp: 'Rudradaman I, who repaired the Sudarshana lake.' },
  { p: 'Which were the three southern kingdoms sung in Sangam poetry?', op: ['Gupta, Pallava and Chalukya', 'Chera, Chola and Pandya', 'Maurya, Shunga and Kanva', 'Satavahana, Shaka and Kushana'], certa: 1, exp: 'Cheras (Kerala), Cholas and Pandyas (Tamil Nadu).' },
  { p: 'Where did the two great schools of Buddhist sculpture of the Kushana era develop?', op: ['Sanchi and Ajanta', 'Taxila and Pataliputra', 'Madurai and Puhar', 'Gandhara and Mathura'], certa: 3, exp: 'Gandhara (Hellenistic style, schist) and Mathura (Indian style, red sandstone).' },
  { p: 'Who was Gautami Balashri?', op: ['A Kushana queen', 'Mother of Gautamiputra Satakarni, who had an inscription engraved at Nashik', 'The wife of Menander', 'The Sangam poetess Avvaiyar'], certa: 1, exp: 'The Nashik inscription describes the victories of her son Gautamiputra Satakarni.' },
  { p: 'What is Mahayana?', op: ['A Jain sect', 'A school of Sanskrit grammar', 'The «Great Vehicle» of Buddhism, with the bodhisattva ideal', 'A Kushana fire cult'], certa: 2, exp: 'Mahayana took shape in this era and travelled along the Silk Road to China.' },
  { p: 'Which Portuguese navigator reached Calicut, on the Malabar coast, in 1498?', op: ['Vasco da Gama', 'Pedro Álvares Cabral', 'Bartolomeu Dias', 'Ferdinand Magellan'], certa: 0, exp: 'Vasco da Gama reached Calicut in May 1498, on a coast where pepper had already been traded with Rome fourteen centuries earlier.' }
